These SVG files are Codicons, Visual Studio Code's icon set.

    Source:    https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-codicons
    Copyright: (c) Microsoft Corporation
    License:   CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Fetched from src/icons/ in that repository, unmodified on disk. EVERY
FILE HERE KEEPS ITS UPSTREAM NAME, which is what makes that sentence
checkable rather than a claim: each one is src/icons/<same name>.svg and
is byte-identical to it. Verify with

    curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/vscode-codicons/\
main/src/icons/<name>.svg | diff - <name>.svg

The review of PR #426 is why this paragraph is this specific. book.svg
arrived hand-drawn, and the blanket "fetched, unmodified" above it was
then false for one of five files — a licensing statement is the wrong
place for an approximation, and the machine-generated coordinate
precision of its neighbours made the odd one out visible on sight. It
was replaced with the real Codicon rather than the claim being narrowed.

The
activitybar package substitutes the documents' fill="currentColor" for a
concrete colour before rasterizing, which is a render-time substitution
and not a change to these files.

CC BY 4.0 permits use and modification, commercial included, and requires
attribution — which is what this file is. Keep it beside the icons.
